      {
        "id": 224521,
        "name": "darkroydante",
        "username": "darkroydante",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/darkroydante/{size}/2044_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-12-04T07:02:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1) Damage increases and reductions are recalculated each time damage is redirected. In your example, the three damage redirected to Stealth Bot is reduced by Stealth Bot's -1, and so Stealth Bot takes 2 damage. Legacy's effects are no longer applied.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2) In every case multiple targets need to take damage, damage&nbsp;happens one target at a time and players choose the order targets take damage in. Ra's Scorched Earth is a great example. Say you are in Insula Primalis and there are 2&nbsp;envrionment cards in play, and say they are 2 Velociraptor Packs with 2 HP each.&nbsp;Ra will deal 2&nbsp;damage to each non-hero target. You select the first&nbsp;Velociraptor Pack and it takes 2 damage, destroying it. Now the second Velociraptor Pack only takes 1 damage becasue there is only 1 envrionment card in play. If you hit the VIllain before all of this, they would take 2 damage. If you hit them after, they would take 1.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Hope that helps!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>edit: Forgot to mention. This&nbsp;<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/clarifications-and-decisions-from-handelabra-christophers-fireside-chats-6773\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">thread</a>&nbsp;is by the developer of the videogame, which catologues major rules clarifications&nbsp;and updates in order of&nbsp;expanions. It's probably one of the best places to check initially if you have a question about a certain card.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:55.930Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
