        "id": 224522,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-12-04T07:21:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Caveats to #1, though:</p>\n<p>If&nbsp;<em>no</em>&nbsp;damage would be dealt, it is not redirected. Say Wraith has used her base power and would be dealt 2 damage. Even if there's something that would force the damage to be redirected (say. Immutus), and it would be more than 0 damage to a different target, it doesn't. Wraith takes 0 and that's the end of it.</p>\n<p>Also, one-time damage reduction, like Wraith's, can be used up even if it is not used. Take the above example: if 3 damage is pointed at Wraith, so that she would take 1, instead Immutus takes 3 but the damage reduction was still \"checked,\" so it's still consumed.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:56.019Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
