        "id": 224524,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-12-04T15:40:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>In addition to the above regarding redirection, don't forget to take Nemesis bonuses into account, if applicable. For example, the Chairman tries to hit Mr Fixer for two points of damage. This is increased to three because of the Nemesis bonus.. But say Fixer has his Pipe Wrench out, thereby reducing all damage to him by one. And he also has Driving Mantis, so when those three points of damage are reduced to two, they suddenly become eligible for redirection and he decides to send them to the Operative. The damage is \"reset\" to its original two points as we are now recalculating for another target. But like Mr Fixer, this one also shares the Chairman's Nemesis bonus so the damage goes back up to three again. Since the Operative has no means of reducing or redirecting this, that's how much she gets hit for :D.</p>\n<p>And for your second question, I think that's been pretty well covered but note that it's not just damage that this applies to - any time <em>any</em> effect will hit multiple targets, players always get to choose the order - nothing is really simultaneous. So for example, say Fanatic/Apostate have just let off an End of Days/Apocalypse while there's a whole bunch of stuff out across all decks. Say Unity is present in this game and has a Bee Bot out. You can destroy all applicable villain and environment things that you want to get blown up, then destroy Bee Bot, who can interrupt the End of Days/Apocalypse by destroying it, which means it's gone and nothing else gets blown up. So other than Bee Bot, everyone gets to keep all their stuff (unless they're someone who <em>likes</em> it when their stuff breaks, like Mainstay or Stuntman or someone, in which case they may ask for that to get popped before the bot) :D.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:56.159Z",
